# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q -l .chktexrc statement.tex
#
# Four warnings are suppressed, each checked hit by hit on 17 August 2026
# rather than assumed, and each with a 100% false-positive rate here:
#
#   9   "`)' expected, found `]'." Fires on the half-open intervals this
#       document quantifies over, $\delta \in (0,1]$ and $\gamma \in (0,1)$.
#       The notation is correct and chktex has no way to know it.
#   17  "Number of `(' doesn't match the number of `)'." The same half-open
#       intervals, counted across the whole file, so it reports once at the
#       end. Follows from 9 and is the same false positive.
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with braces." Fires on
#       $\bigl(...\bigr)_{j}$ and $(\bits^{*})^{2}$, where the sub- and
#       superscripts attach to the delimiter exactly as intended.
#   24  "Delete this space to maintain correct pagereferences." Fires on
#       \label{...} sitting on its own line after \begin{...}, which is this
#       file's convention and the same one the Uber paper suppresses it for.
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 17 August 2026 the file is clean under this
# config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n9
    -n17
    -n3
    -n24
}
